 ### [Screen-space Post-processing](3621-screen-space-post-processing.md)
-Screen-space post-processing is a full-screen rendering stage that applies aspect-ratio preserving UV covering, luminance-based bright passes, color grading, spatial blurring, and dithering to a scene texture to produce a display-ready image. It differs from direct volume compositing methods by operating entirely in screen space on the final display image rather than during ray traversal, allowing for complex aesthetic effects like bloom and vignette without modifying the volume rendering pipeline. See [Screen-space Post-processing](3621-screen-space-post-processing.md).
