 ### [Layer-Centric Volume Rendering Framework](6994-layer-centric-volume-rendering-framework.md)
-The Layer-Centric Volume Rendering Framework is a visualization architecture that constructs the final image by compositing multiple distinct renderings, each treated as an independent layer. It solves the rigidity of traditional single-pass volume rendering by segmenting the workflow into a rendering phase for small regions of interest and a subsequent compositing phase. This approach provides a rich set of 2D operators and interactions, allowing for greater freedom and more intuitive user interaction compared to standard volume rendering techniques. See [Layer-Centric Volume Rendering Framework](6994-layer-centric-volume-rendering-framework.md).
