 ### [MAB Compositing with Gaze-Contingent Blending](8211-mab-compositing-with-gaze-contingent-blending.md)
-MAB compositing is a gaze-contingent rendering technique that maps framebuffer fragments to a Multi-Anchor Buffer (MAB) to retrieve and blend color values from different resolution levels based on the distance to the center of gaze. It solves the performance bottleneck in immersive VR volume rendering by dynamically adjusting resolution distribution to maintain high frame rates, thereby preventing cybersickness caused by performance fluctuations. Unlike standard fixed-resolution ray casting, it blends multiple resolution levels simultaneously using a smooth-step function to ensure unnoticeable transitions between detail levels. See [MAB Compositing with Gaze-Contingent Blending](8211-mab-compositing-with-gaze-contingent-blending.md).
