 ### [Multi-view image blending](9831-multi-view-image-blending.md)
-Multi-view image blending reduces artifacts caused by single-view fading, such as ghosting and transparency variation, by combining a set of images taken from various view angles. It sets itself apart from single-texture approaches by requiring the selection and blending of at least three textures, trading increased rendering cost for improved visual fidelity across viewpoints. See [Multi-view image blending](9831-multi-view-image-blending.md).
