 ### [Dynamic Job-Scheduling for Grid Volume Rendering](10585-dynamic-job-scheduling-for-grid-volume-rendering.md)
-Dynamic Job-Scheduling for Grid Volume Rendering is a distributed rendering technique that determines the processing order of sub-volumes based on their real-time visibility rather than a static sequence. It solves the bottleneck caused by heterogeneous agent speeds in grid computing, where static sequential scheduling forces fast agents to wait for slow agents to complete prior steps. By using obstacle-flags to track obscuration, the method allows agents to immediately process newly visible sub-volumes, significantly improving efficiency over sequential approaches. See [Dynamic Job-Scheduling for Grid Volume Rendering](10585-dynamic-job-scheduling-for-grid-volume-rendering.md).
