 ### [HardSoftRas Blending](10747-hardsoftras-blending.md)
-HardSoftRas Blending is a pixel-wise compositing strategy for differentiable rendering that distinguishes between edge pixels (silhouettes and vertical surfaces) and non-edge pixels to balance anti-aliasing with texture sharpness. Unlike SoftRas, which blends all faces in non-edge regions, HardSoftRas retains the most frontal color for non-edges while applying weighted averaging for edges, thereby maintaining sharp textures inside silhouettes and generating far-range gradients around boundaries. See [HardSoftRas Blending](10747-hardsoftras-blending.md).
